  "body": "## What changed\n\n- This PR adds the catalog case `examples/catalog/edm/sinker`. It is the first case in the `edm` family.\n- The model is a 60 x 40 x 25 mm block with one blind rectangular cavity, 20 x 12 x 8 mm, centred at (5, 0). The model is original. `model/gen_sinker_obj.py` generates it.\n- `build.camscript` loads the shipped machine `Sinker EDM 3-axis (template)`.\n  It adds two conditions (`R1` rough, `F1` finish) and the sinker code words with `edit_machine`.\n  The values and the words are invented. The script and the README say so.\n- `electrode_from_faces` makes the electrode `E-19.5x11.5` from the cavity floor and four walls, with the `R1` undersize (0.25 mm per side).\n- The case has two operations:\n  - `Rough burn` (Sinker Burn, `R1`, pass `rough`): one servo block, `M101 Z17.25 F50.`.\n  - `Side burn +X` (Sinker Side Burn, `F1`): `M101 Z17.03 F50.`, then `M102 X5.22 ...` and `M102 X5. ...`.\n- The post is `Sinker EDM (ISO)`, set with `add_setup` and `set_setup_post`.\n- `cargo xtask catalog` added the case link to the Sinker Burn and Sinker Side Burn sections of `site/content/guide/operations/operations-edm.md`.\n- `docs/decisions/2872-sinker-catalog.md` records the choices.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe issue asks for an example case for the two sinker kinds. The earlier attempt stopped because the post refused Sinker Side Burn (#3001). #3001 is closed. The post now posts a side burn when the machine states the `side` code.\n\n## Tests\n\nCommands and results on head `23e11a965` (base `b2afd64ed`):\n\n- Pins (new, `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_edm_sinker.rs`):\n  - `catalog_edm_sinker::regenerates`\n  - `catalog_edm_sinker::rebuilds`\n  - `sinker_case_posts_the_burn_and_the_side_burn`: checks the two sections in order, the condition of each section, the depth of each servo burn, and the two lateral blocks (out to `X5.22`, back to `X5.`, `Y` and `Z` constant). It also checks that the straight burn has no lateral block.\n- Red before the case: all three pins failed (`edm/sinker: missing model/`, and `sinker.nc: No such file or directory`).\n- Mutation: I removed the return block `M102 X5. ...` from `sinker.nc`. All three pins failed (`out to the wall and back: left 1, right 2`, and the byte compare of `regenerates` and `rebuilds`). I restored the file. All three pins passed.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: all 16 cases checked, `edm/sinker` included.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 10 steps, 0 failed (app build, `catalog_groove_part_off`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `first_4axis_part`, `first_part_programs`, `first_router_part`, `tilt_basis_compat`).\n  - The first run had a build fault (`E0460` on `thiserror`) from a seeded target. `cargo clean -p camcraft-app -p thiserror` cleared it. The second run was green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `contract::every_case_has_two_named_test_results`: passes with the new case.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- New: `examples/catalog/edm/sinker/sinker.nc` and `sinker.camproj`. No existing program, `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lane was not run. `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` reaches one step, `app heavy: example_catalog`. That step runs only the ignored cases `2d/adaptive-pocket` and `2d/slots`. This PR does not change them. The new case is not ignored and ran in the quick gate. No production code changed.\n- The light lane was not run. Its plan has only motion and pocket twins, which this diff does not reach.\n- No screenshots. The case changes no UI.\n- The program uses invented code words. It was not run on a real EDM control.\n- `upstream/main` moved to `c79c9b24f` during the work. The new commits change UI files and docs only. The branch merges cleanly with it (`git merge-tree`).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- None. No open PR changes `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`, `examples/catalog/edm/` or `operations-edm.md`.\n\nChangelog: Example case `edm/sinker`: a rough Sinker Burn and a Sinker Side Burn of one cavity, on the sinker EDM template.\n\nFixes #2872\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
